# Gradle output directories, matched by position rather than by name.
#
# `**/build/` looks like the obvious pattern and is a trap: it also matches the Java package
# `gov/niemplatform/build/`, which silently removes the canonical model's code generator from the
# build context. The image then builds far enough to fail with "plugin implementation class not
# found", which points nowhere near the cause.
#
# A Gradle project directory is at depth 0, 1 or 2 here, so its build/ is too. A package path is
# deeper, and never matches.
/build
/*/build
/*/*/build
.gradle/

# Local tooling and editor state.
.idea/
.vscode/
.zen/
*.iml

# History is large and the build does not read it.
.git/
.github/

# Documentation and demos are not inputs to the platform binary.
docs/
demo/
*.md
